<%# locals: (current_workspace:) -%>
<%# Desktop workspace-sidebar wrapper — provides the <aside> landmark
    and the boxed sidebar visual chrome. Contents (the workspace switcher,
    which carries identity, plus the nav items) live in
    _workspace_sidebar_items.html.erb. Below md, the same items source instead
    renders as an in-page section-nav strip (see _section_nav_strip) — not
    this <aside>.

    Sticky because the switcher lives here rather than in the header: a tenant
    indicator that scrolls away is the argument that retired the old context
    banner, and it would apply just as well to this. The 4rem offset and height
    both track the header's inner h-16 (_header) — change that and these must
    move with it. The 1px the header's border adds is hidden behind the header
    itself, which paints above (z-40).

    The Settings hub's own sidebar (_settings_sidebar) is sticky to match. -%>
<aside aria-label="<%= t("workspaces.sidebar.aria_label") %>"
       class="w-64 shrink-0 px-4 pt-4 pb-6 border-r border-border bg-surface
              md:sticky md:top-16 md:h-[calc(100dvh-4rem)] md:overflow-y-auto">
  <%= render "shared/workspace_sidebar_items",
        current_workspace: current_workspace %>
</aside>
